    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>g(a)</m>, below.  It may be to
your advantage to simplify before differentiating.</p>
<p><m>g(a) = \tan(\arctan(3 a))</m></p>
<p><m>g'(a) =</m> <fillin characters="65" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><em>(Your answer should be in simplified form.)</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\arctan(\tan(3 a)) = 3 a</m>, so 
<m>g'(a) = 3</m>.



</solution>
